    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0c9efe0d_1c2c059e",
        "filename": "net/tetheroffload/control/1.0/IOffloadControl.hal",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 112,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000866
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-31T17:52:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it would be helpful to have a method that does not reset the stats when invoked so that you can get incremental stats from a HAL if you wanted.  With just this method, you are shifting responsibility to the client to aggregate data from multiple calls to the stats.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 112,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 112,
        "endChar": 89
      },
      "revId": "8304b42077e87e30c4046e6fc4054b39bfb4eb3d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f19deddf_96f857a2",
        "filename": "net/tetheroffload/control/1.0/IOffloadControl.hal",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 112,
      "author": {
        "id": 1062130
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-31T21:50:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is done, because the management process maintains all statistics on disk in a persistent storage. The stats are pulled from hardware and the server does not maintain any state for these statistics. The implication of the statistics for an interface may change between a lifecycle of a data call and therefore its best its caller knows when to pull this information and how to attribute its cost. Any state or smarts in the server may indirectly require the server to understand how the caller wants to count these statistics. A pull and clear API keeps the interface straight forward without creating additional dependency of how to interpret these interface statistics between the client and server.",
      "parentUuid": "0c9efe0d_1c2c059e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 112,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 112,
        "endChar": 89
      },
      "revId": "8304b42077e87e30c4046e6fc4054b39bfb4eb3d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
